# Docker build-context ignore (applies to every image built with context `..`,
# i.e. both docker/api.Dockerfile and docker/frontend.Dockerfile).
#
# Goal: send only the sources the Dockerfiles actually COPY (backend/, frontend/
# sources + package*.json, docker/nginx.conf) and let each image restore/build
# fresh inside the container. This keeps the context small and prevents a host
# (Windows) node_modules from overlaying the alpine `npm ci` output (esbuild
# win32 vs linux-musl native-binary mismatch).

# Version control / tooling metadata
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# Node / Angular artifacts - the frontend image runs `npm ci` + `npm run build`
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.angular

# .NET build artifacts - the API image runs `dotnet restore` + `dotnet publish`
**/bin
**/obj

# Logs
*.log
**/*.log

# Legacy source trees retired by the migration (not consumed by any Dockerfile COPY)
Library
Website

# Local QA/agent artifacts (screenshots, recordings) - never part of a runtime image
blitzy
